FailAt 21
; ZZScreensaverR_GuardTest - checks that ZZScreensaverR 1.0 ends when its screen is no longer in front.
; One run of the 64 x 48 grid. After 300 frames (about five seconds) the program sends its own
; screen to the back: the Workbench shows and the program must end at once. Should it not, the run
; ends by itself 60 frames later. Nothing to type; do not touch the mouse or the keyboard.
; Run ZZScreensaverR_Test first. Switch off any screen blanker of another program first.
; In the drawer of ZZScreensaverR, from a Shell there:
;      Execute ZZScreensaverR_GuardTest
; Everything goes to zzsr_guard.txt in that drawer.
Echo "=== ZZScreensaverR 1.0 guard test ===" >zzsr_guard.txt
Version ZZScreensaverR >>zzsr_guard.txt
Echo "=== PRESET 2 grid 64x48, screen to back after 300 frames ===" >>zzsr_guard.txt
ZZScreensaverR 360 PRESET 2 TOBACK 300 DEBUG >>zzsr_guard.txt
If WARN
  Echo "GUARD RUN FAILED" >>zzsr_guard.txt
  Echo "ZZScreensaverR_GuardTest: run failed. See zzsr_guard.txt"
  Quit 10
EndIf
Echo "=== ZZScreensaverR 1.0 guard test done ===" >>zzsr_guard.txt
Echo "ZZScreensaverR_GuardTest done: see zzsr_guard.txt"
